WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.629
- She got a lucky one.

00:00:01.629 --> 00:00:02.710
She gonna go home, get lucky.

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:04.268
- X-rated, cut that out.

00:00:04.268 --> 00:00:06.126
- [Woman] Dumplings.

00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:08.203
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.203 --> 00:00:09.940
- Hi, nice to meet you.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.390
My name's Lily Yang and I am from Taiwan.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.140
So I'm gonna show you how to make Chinese

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.050
dumpling Taiwan style.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.550
Okay, let's get started.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:23.550
So usually I marinate with
the soy sauce and not much,

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.620
because we got to put some salt,

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.160
so you don't want too much soy sauce,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.240
add some white pepper,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.670
and then put a little bit ginger in there.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.260
Ginger is good for the body.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.330
When you have a cold, as
my grandmother would say,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.700
take away your cold.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.310
So then you wanna set this aside.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.510
For 10, 15 minutes,

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.680
and then you wanna drop your
green chopped vegetables,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.330
about two-thirds of the meat

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.050
and one-third of the vegetable,

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.370
and then just kind of mix

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.203
together.

00:00:51.203 --> 00:00:54.207
- First time I see anyone
using bok choy in the dumpling.

00:00:54.207 --> 00:00:55.130
- Oh, the first time for me too.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:58.120
But I never, never see anybody do that.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.120
- I usually don't use the Chinese cabbage

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.470
because too much water.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:04.040
You blow the dumpling skin.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.080
And then I put some wine in there

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.810
just to make it taste good.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:08.880
So what you do is,

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.760
because it is a machine make skin,

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.980
so you need to use
water to dip on the side

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.330
so you would stick it together.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:18.200
So when we were a kid, they
can wrap all kind of shape.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.990
But my grandmother always
make like Chinese money.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.380
It's nice, right?

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.683
- The way she's folding it,

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.740
it's so cute.
- Perfect.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.000
- And then you put the
almond in the center.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.250
You can hide it, this is
like secret ingredient.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.590
You don't wanna tell anybody.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.730
So the lucky person, that's
just going to have the almond

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.180
in the center.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.320
And when they bite it, it's crunchy.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.070
- I wish my husband would do that

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.870
and put a diamond ring in it.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.210
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.750
- So I'm ready to put in the boiled water.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.500
You can just slowly pull it in there.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.460
Okay. And then you wanna make
sure you stir a little bit.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.620
You don't want them stuck
in the bottom and then

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.130
I just pour another cup of water.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.110
And then I just put the cover.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.058
When the dumpling is ready,
they will float on top.

00:02:00.058 --> 00:02:02.830
And meanwhile I can just mix the sauce.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.757
Soy sauce and then I
have a little sesame oil,

00:02:05.757 --> 00:02:08.440
put a little wine there
just for the taste.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.640
Some people like a lot
of wine so they can get

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:11.473
a little buzz.

00:02:11.473 --> 00:02:14.820
Okay, and then I have to
put little chive in there

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.420
and then garlic and ginger.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.150
And then I usually put a little jalapeno,

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.650
actually this is not
Chinese, just for the taste.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.050
That's your dipping sauce.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.940
So they all blow up like this.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.160
Okay, when they look like little bubbles.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.200
So meanwhile I just put some oil,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.270
because if you don't finish it right away,

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.724
they stick it together.

00:02:33.724 --> 00:02:34.810
The thing about my shape,

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.000
you can even stand up.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.005
Look at that!

00:02:37.005 --> 00:02:38.082
(laughing)

00:02:38.082 --> 00:02:40.665
(upbeat music)

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.820
- My name is XiaoZhe Liu, I
came from mainland of China

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.870
called Shenyang, it's Northeast.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.540
First of all, I'm gonna soak a spice.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.180
Gets rid for the fishy
smell from the meat.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.620
Spice, green onion, and ginger,

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.950
and I'm gonna put hot water inside.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:03.237
Any grandma make dumpling,
they can make pork dumpling.

00:03:03.237 --> 00:03:04.720
But lamb is difficult.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.540
You got to cook perfect.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.050
Otherwise it doesn't taste good.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.090
- Honestly, I only know how to use pork.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.970
I don't even know how to use chicken.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.520
- Next, I'm gonna making a dough.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:16.030
Only flour and raise warm water.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.830
You know, people can use
the hot water, cold water.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:19.970
Me prefer the warm water,

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.300
that way the though is soft,

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.820
and not too soft and not too hard

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.420
is perfect condition.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:26.660
I think,

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:27.493
okay now.

00:03:27.493 --> 00:03:31.960
So far, now I like it to
sleep like 20 minutes.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.370
But normally like two hours,
three hours is better.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.920
Cover it tight.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.500
Don't let moisture, go out.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.280
- So much mess, what the heck?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.977
You work all day and
you come home do this?

00:03:41.977 --> 00:03:44.120
Forget it. (laughing)

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.040
- Morning time, you just use
the store bought wrapper.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.130
- Okay, next step.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.290
I'm gonna put the cooking
wine into the meat,

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.170
soy sauce, this is my special one,

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.040
low salt, but more tasty.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:56.873
Look good, too.

00:03:56.873 --> 00:03:58.420
Little bit salt.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.730
This called massage the lamb..

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.620
Then next step, make
this, it's spicy water.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.480
So this water can kill the fishy smell.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.720
I call the fishy smell.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.410
Now is the fun part.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:12.690
You know, you gotta do the
clockwise or counter clockwise.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.650
One direction, you don't mix it.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.630
You don't like do this one, this one,

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.490
you don't do that.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.507
Then when I was kid, I see
my mom do this all time.

00:04:20.507 --> 00:04:21.560
And I try to help.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.410
I try to do the different way.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.753
My mom said, no, no, you cannot do that.

00:04:24.753 --> 00:04:25.880
I said, why?

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.290
You mess up the lamb!

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.760
I said, why?
No, not tasty.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.640
Why? I don't ask me
why too many questions.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:33.473
It's just not good.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.442
Okay. I said, okay. (beep)

00:04:35.442 --> 00:04:36.275
I just watch and eat.

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:37.933
This is the exercise too, work out.

00:04:39.175 --> 00:04:42.060
You know, this meat the perfect time.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.610
Not too much watery and not dry.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.560
That's the perfect.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.230
Now I'll mix the onion,
I like red onion better.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.720
White onion a little sweet,
but red onion is spicy.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:53.670
- That's a lot of onion.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.630
- And it has a lot of water too.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:58.430
And then she already dumped the water in.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.263
- And the cucumber.

00:04:59.263 --> 00:05:02.620
Cucumber make the
dumpling like fresh smell

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.300
Sesame oil, a little bit.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.020
This is olive oil.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.750
They can lock the water
of the vegetables inside.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:09.950
That's all for the meat.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:14.810
Now I'm taking out of
the top, make the skin.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.620
Oh, well you're good.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:21.160
Got to use one thumb into press,

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.050
and then one hand, you
know, roll it like this.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.630
After you do the dumpling,
your thumb, you know

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.090
you'll be sore.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.943
Then you make a hole inside
and you just do like this.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.320
I see lot of people cut it little pieces.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.310
I prefer like use my hand.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:42.750
Like a piece of art.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:43.710
It's fun.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.130
I enjoy it.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.710
Now I put a little dry flour on the top.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:50.980
So when you make the skin, it
doesn't stick on the board.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.600
Huh? I use the stick to make the skin.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.510
- She does it so professionally.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:59.400
Wow. Looks so thin, too.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.738
- See the way you go to roll this out.

00:06:01.738 --> 00:06:02.571
This all very fast.

00:06:02.571 --> 00:06:04.990
Otherwise too much here until last there

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.410
the center is a little hard.

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.600
You don't go all the through,

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.030
otherwise the dumpling will burst.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:10.268
Finished!

00:06:10.268 --> 00:06:11.530
Filling in,

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:12.700
when I was kid, I told you

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.640
my grandma make the dumpling like this.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.350
I said, mom, grandma look like a bug.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.300
I don't want to eat it.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.580
She said, you gotta eat it.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:20.690
After I cook it,

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:23.380
you'll feel the bug delicious.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.390
Look, pretty or not?

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:27.003
Now's the steam dumpling time.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.960
Okay, that's enough.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.310
Put on the top.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.390
You'll count 13 minutes

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:39.070
and meantime I can make garlic sauce.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.953
First of all, put a
garlic and then soy sauce.

00:06:43.165 --> 00:06:46.250
Okay, and then sesame oil and then mix it.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.023
Okay, let's check out the product.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:51.970
Who want try it?

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.553
(upbeat music)

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.250
- Hi, my name is Susana Tan

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.320
and I'm from Hong Kong.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.480
- Today I will be making
truffle dumplings.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.730
- Do you know how to spell truffle?

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.280
- It's kind of expensive, no?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.330
- Okay, first of all,

00:07:08.591 --> 00:07:10.220
I have half a pound of pork here

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.380
and I have a piece of ginger

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.780
and I'm going to add some water to it.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.600
So I let this sit,

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:20.018
while I put the rest of
the ingredients in it.

00:07:20.018 --> 00:07:24.180
So I have a teaspoon of oyster sauce,

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:29.180
a teaspoon of soy sauce,
and a pinch of pepper.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.480
And then I will add some truffle salt.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.531
- What is that?

00:07:34.531 --> 00:07:35.364
- Maybe MSG?

00:07:35.364 --> 00:07:37.960
- Oh, don't put MSG, don't put that!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:41.800
- Truffle pate, you can add
as much as you can, honestly.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.600
And the truffle oil,

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.083
I'm going to strain the ginger water.

00:07:47.286 --> 00:07:49.370
And now I'm gonna mix it all together.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:52.130
I just loosen it up in the liquid

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:55.180
until I get the consistency that I want.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:56.410
I do not knead it,

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.630
because personally if I knead it,

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:02.460
I find that feeling
becomes very thick and hard

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.640
after you cook them.

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.980
And now I will just add the chives.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:08.240
I do not use a lot of chives

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:11.890
because chives has its
distinctive taste to it.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:15.020
And because this is a truffle dumpling,

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.300
you do not want the chives to cover

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.850
the taste of the truffle.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:19.683
Yeah.

00:08:19.683 --> 00:08:20.516
Voila!

00:08:20.516 --> 00:08:21.910
So now I'm going to wrap it.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:26.910
I cannot fold it like how
other people can really fast.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:29.400
I am pretty slow in doing this,

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.760
but patient pays, worth the wait.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.800
I like to make eight folds on my dumpling

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.280
because eight is very
auspicious for the Chinese.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.150
Eight means prosperity.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:41.730
And when you make the dumplings,

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:45.480
it's supposed to be in the shape
of a Chinese golden nugget,

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.020
just like this.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:50.540
Like a half moon so that's how it is.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.240
I'm all ready to fry them.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.600
I'll add a little oil,
just a little bit first.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.570
It's not hot yet so we
can just swirl it around

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.230
so that the bottom has a bit of oil.

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.800
Arrange it nicely,

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:05.240
but make sure that it's
not touching each other.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.560
Okay, now that it's a little
bit sizzling, not a lot,

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:11.270
I can add the water to it around the side.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:13.300
You can hear it sizzles a little bit

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.213
and I'm going to cover it
with the water, like steaming,

00:09:16.213 --> 00:09:18.340
like half steaming, half boiling.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:19.840
- Fry's most delicious.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:20.673
But fry,

00:09:20.673 --> 00:09:22.690
you gotta have a very good skills.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:26.700
- Okay, now that you see the
water has evaporated a lot,

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:31.040
you can add the oil so that
we are gonna fry the bottom

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:33.820
of it so it becomes crispy.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:37.350
Okay. Sounds very good.
It looks pretty much done.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:39.440
Let's see how crispy looks.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:41.910
It's golden brown.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.500
Mm. It smells good. It's gotta taste good.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.889
And that's it. Here it is.

00:09:46.889 --> 00:09:49.472
(upbeat music)

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:53.546
- Party time girl.

00:09:53.546 --> 00:09:54.379
- Yeah.

00:09:54.379 --> 00:09:55.212
- It's dumplings.

00:09:55.212 --> 00:09:56.510
- Let me try Lily, yours first.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:57.659
- Right.

00:09:57.659 --> 00:09:58.492
- First.

00:09:58.492 --> 00:09:59.325
- Okay.

00:09:59.325 --> 00:10:00.158
- Oh, so good

00:10:00.158 --> 00:10:00.991
- Girl.

00:10:00.991 --> 00:10:01.824
- So juicy.

00:10:01.824 --> 00:10:02.657
- Can I try yours?

00:10:02.657 --> 00:10:03.490
- Yes, of course.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.760
Please, please, please, please.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:05.771
Well?

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:07.076
- You use very expensive oil.

00:10:07.076 --> 00:10:08.930
(laughing)

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.136
- Okay. I'll try yours, Ping.

00:10:11.136 --> 00:10:12.044
- Good?

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:13.220
Tell me the truth.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.180
- First time I have lamb.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.240
- In your whole life?

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.410
- In my whole life.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:18.340
- I'm so proud.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.189
- First time.

00:10:19.189 --> 00:10:20.022
- I'm so proud.

00:10:20.022 --> 00:10:21.260
- It is so good.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.653
- And why, why your girls
don't make the dough?

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:26.484
- Honestly, I don't
know how to make dough.

00:10:26.484 --> 00:10:27.990
- Oh, how about you?

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:29.220
- I know how to do it.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:30.250
- You just don't wanna do it.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.015
- Yeah, because it's too much work.

00:10:32.015 --> 00:10:34.036
(laughing)

00:10:34.036 --> 00:10:35.090
- Lazy, lazy girls.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.294
- The dough tastes good
if you made your own.

00:10:37.294 --> 00:10:38.170
- Right?

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:39.003
- Different taste.

00:10:39.003 --> 00:10:39.836
- Yeah. It tastes different.

00:10:39.836 --> 00:10:41.360
- It's not only the lamb.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.887
I think it's the soul.

00:10:42.887 --> 00:10:43.720
My soul.

00:10:44.745 --> 00:10:45.578
- Okay.

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:46.411
- My soul.

00:10:48.047 --> 00:10:49.640
- She got dancing dumpling.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:50.940
- What is that crunchy thing in it?

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:52.425
- You got almond?

00:10:52.425 --> 00:10:53.495
- Oh I see!

00:10:53.495 --> 00:10:55.305
- You the lucky one!

00:10:55.305 --> 00:10:57.207
- Thanks for watching!

00:10:57.207 --> 00:10:59.790
(upbeat music)

